# Regex literal flags roundtrip

Verifies the `i` case-insensitive flag and the `g` global flag survive parsing
and print back verbatim as part of the literal text.

>>> source
const insensitive: regex = /hello/i
print(insensitive)
const combined: regex = /hello/gi
print(combined)

<<< stdout
/hello/i
/hello/gi

<<< stderr
